---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import UnderConstruction from '../components/UnderConstruction.astro';
---

<Base title="JDN">
  <div class="heading">
    <h1><b>JDN</b></h1>
  </div>
  <hr />
  <div class="introduction">
    <table>
      <tr>
        <td>
          <img class="portrait" src="./Portrait.jpeg" alt="Portrait of Jayden Chan" />
        </td>
        <td class="intro-text">
          <p>
            I've never seen much point describing someone by a single title. What good does it do to tell me that, say, <a class="ext" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jim_Thorpe" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Jim Thorpe</a> was an American athlete? I would find it more interesting if one told me he was also a background actor, construction worker, a doorman, a security guard, a ditchdigger; briefly sailed for the <a class="ext" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Merchant_Marine" target="_blank" rel="noopener">United States Merchant Marine</a>; had Native American heritage and experience racism for that reason. <a class="ext" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jim_Thorpe#Later_life,_film_career,_and_death" target="_blank" rel="noopener">(Yes, all this is true!)</a>
          </p>
          <p>
            Indeed, I think everyone should be described beyond a couple of sentences. This reason is why I struggle to call myself just a <i>musician</i>, or an <i>IBDP student</i>. It would be a shame to try so many new things and <a class="pill" href="./experience.html" style="background-color: #2DB23A;">experiences</a> and not let it change who I am in any way. People aren't meant to be introduced like that.
          </p>
          <p>
            If I could, I would rather call myself a 16 year old human being who studies the IBDP, performs and writes <a class="pill" href="./music.html" style="background-color: #7A4FBF;">music</a> as a side hustle, who also practices first aid and scouting, and also teaches coding to primary school students, and also wrote a children's book and dressed up as Father Christmas that one time.
          </p>
          <p>
            This website is me doing that, in internet form. Please enjoy this amalgamation of <a class="pill" href="./gallery.html" style="background-color: #1C99CE;">projects</a> old and new that I think are cool enough to share with the world wide web.
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  </div>
  <hr />
  <div class="stuffIdo">
    <h2 class="heading"><b>Stuff I Do</b></h2>
    <UnderConstruction caption="Stuff is being done. Mostly this sign." />
  </div>
  <div class="goodbye">
    <button class="original-btn" id="open-warning">View the original website</button>
  </div>
  <dialog id="original-warning" class="warning">
    <p>The website you will see was made when I was 12, before coders everywhere got lazy and started vibe coding. It is dangerously broken, ugly, and straight up cringe.</p>
    <p>You have been warned...</p>
    <div class="warning-actions">
      <button class="back-btn" id="close-warning">Take me back</button>
      <a class="ready-btn" href="./original/index.html">I am ready</a>
    </div>
  </dialog>
  <script is:inline>
    const dialog = document.getElementById('original-warning');
    document.getElementById('open-warning').addEventListener('click', () => dialog.showModal());
    document.getElementById('close-warning').addEventListener('click', () => dialog.close());
  </script>
</Base>


<style is:global>
  body {
    background: linear-gradient(-45deg, #ee7752, #e73c7e, #23a6d5, #23d5ab);
    background-size: 400% 400%;
    animation: gradient 15s ease infinite;
    min-height: 100vh;
  }

  @keyframes gradient {
    0% { background-position: 0% 50%; }
    50% { background-position: 100% 50%; }
    100% { background-position: 0% 50%; }
  }
</style>

<style>
  .heading {
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 50px;
    font-family: 'Bebas Neue', cursive;
  }

  div {
    margin: 5px;
    padding: 0px;
  }

  .portrait {
    width: 600px;
    max-width: 40vw;
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
  }

  .intro-text {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  /* Links to other websites: plain underlined text. */
  .ext {
    color: white;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }
  .ext:hover {
    opacity: 0.8;
  }

  /* The coloured inline links to the other pages. They used to be <button>s
     with onclick handlers; real links look the same and work without JavaScript. */
  .pill {
    padding: 1px 4px;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: white;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .goodbye {
    text-align: center;
    margin: 32px 0 64px;
  }
  .original-btn {
    background-color: white;
    color: #111;
    font-family: 'Poppins', sans-serif;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 18px;
    padding: 12px 24px;
    border: none;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .original-btn:hover {
    opacity: 0.85;
  }

  .warning {
    max-width: 460px;
    width: calc(100% - 32px);
    border: 4px solid #FFC83D;
    background: #111;
    color: white;
    padding: 24px;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .warning::backdrop {
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6);
  }
  .warning-actions {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: flex-end;
    gap: 12px;
    margin: 16px 0 0;
  }
  .back-btn,
  .ready-btn {
    font-family: 'Poppins', sans-serif;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 15px;
    padding: 8px 16px;
    cursor: pointer;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .back-btn {
    background: transparent;
    color: white;
    border: 2px solid white;
  }
  .ready-btn {
    background: #FFC83D;
    color: #111;
  }
</style>
